  "articleBody": "Ripping out a worn shower enclosure seems straightforward, but minor demolition oversights can lead to major structural repairs down the line. Protecting your home requires a cautious, methodical approach.\n\nCommon Mistakes to Avoid:\n- Treating removal as pure cosmetic work: Yanking out surrounds without checking for underlying framing rot leaves soft, decayed wood in place.\n- Failing to verify water shutoffs: Forgetting to relieve line pressure before unthreading valves can result in sudden water damage inside the wall.\n- Reusing degraded subfloors: Installing a new shower pan over water-softened plywood leads to flexing, cracked grout, and future leaks. Always replace compromised subfloor sheets.\n- Skipping drain and pan leak tests: Closing up the surrounding walls before testing the new drain connection risks hidden leaks beneath your finished tile.\n- Damaging adjacent electrical runs: Tearing into wall cavities blindly can sever wiring feeding bathroom outlets or lighting.\n\nWhen you discover rotted studs, rusted plumbing, or extensive mold during demo, getting a skilled contractor involved protects your property. HH Remodeling LLC specializes in bathroom renovations, handling demolition, framing repairs, drywall, and custom tile installation from start to finish. Call Abraham Becerra at 303-505-0866 to discuss your shower removal project.",
